meta {
  name: Create Style
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/styles
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "default_point_style",
    "sldContent": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?><StyledLayerDescriptor xmlns=\"http://www.opengis.net/sld\" xmlns:ogc=\"http://www.opengis.net/ogc\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" version=\"1.0.0\"><NamedLayer><Name>default_point_style</Name><UserStyle><FeatureTypeStyle><Rule><PointSymbolizer><Graphic><Mark><WellKnownName>circle</WellKnownName><Fill><CssParameter name=\"fill\">#1e5ba8</CssParameter></Fill></Mark><Size>8</Size></Graphic></PointSymbolizer></Rule></FeatureTypeStyle></UserStyle></NamedLayer></StyledLayerDescriptor>"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('styleId', res.body.id);
    bru.setVar('defaultStyleId', res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` is set.

  **Expected Response:** 201 Created, body contains `id`, `name`, and the persisted `sldContent`.

  **Post-condition:** Save `styleId` and `defaultStyleId` from `body.id`. `defaultStyleId` is the sticky reference used as `defaultStyleId` in `layers/create-layer.bru`.

  **Validation:** `name` must match the SafeNames pattern `[A-Za-z0-9_-]+` and be unique within the parent DataSet. The backend only enforces `@NotBlank` on `sldContent` — the test payload uses a minimal SLD 1.0.0 shell sufficient for backend CRUD round-trips. Replace with a full SLD body if exercising the GeoServer upload step.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | Style record created in `portal_backend` DB, linked to the DataSet |
  | Config Adapter | — (style is uploaded to GeoServer when the parent DataSet is released) |
  | External System | — |
}
